      <groundspeak:logs>
        <groundspeak:log id="685900359">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-13T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6252216">hunthikers</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP185 Calgary - Oakridge

Out this afternoon for a few caps and caches near the Glenmore reservoir while Mrs Hunthikers and Mr Foothills Scrambler went for their inaugural sail of the season. After we dropped them off we headed to the S side with Mrs Foothills Scrambler for a geowalk. This cap was our first stop. Some of the fence is down, but we found the key divot, blew away some dirt and got what we needed. TFTC. &lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="684638343">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-05-06T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="6304346">sapien</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP185 Calgary - Oakridge

N 50° 58.674 W 114° 08.278&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This area looked vaguely familiar to me.  That's because I was actually here with a couple of my caching friends right after I started caching a few years ago but I didn't log it then.  So here I am back again today for it.  This turned out to be my last cap of the day, and most likely my last one before the change.  So one last final shout-out and BIG thank you to OFTH for starting and maintaining this cache for all these years.  Hopefully it'll be around for many more so that all cachers, new and old, get to enjoy it as well.  TFTBC.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="682008486">
