          <groundspeak:finder id="540154">One Bad Ant</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP185 Oakridge	&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the multiple finds becoming extinct, I suppose I should keep an eye out for brass caps. A fun walk and find. Thanks OFTH.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="679163612">
          <groundspeak:date>2017-04-18T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="1636194">behmSquad</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BCP185 Calgary - Oakridge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day #4 of cappapalooza.  I only had time for a couple today, but they were both good challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On approach, I really didn't think I was going to find this one.  Enmax has the whole road under construction including regrading the entire shoulder.  There were no tell tale divots to search.  Much of the fence is still in place, but the reference utility pole is nowhere in sight.  Using CR's log, I was able focus my search relative to the fence.  And after just a little bit of probing, I got lucky.  Digging down several inches confirmed my find.  Thanks for the cap.&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
